  {"comment":"SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT. A sheet joined with its mirror image where a bend crosses the mirror plane (mitcad#1558): rules t=2, r=3, K=0.3, the reference side the front. A 60 x 20 Face at y = 50..70 folded 90 degrees up at x = 0 (bend line): the panels 30 - c long with c = 0.9 pi, half the bend allowance (pi/2)(r + K t), the bend 80 pi; 2400 - 72 pi + 80 pi = 2400 + 8 pi. Mirrored with Join about its wall at y = 70, which the bend crosses: the panels and the bend meet their images along the plane, the bend's image on the bend's cylinder, and the sheet is one valid sheet of three charts and one bend, 4800 + 16 pi, x = -30 .. 5 - c, y = 50..90, z = 0 .. 35 - c; its Flat Pattern is the 60 x 40 blank at x = -30..30, y = 50..90. Before the fix the two bends stayed two domains meeting at the plane and the join failed (an empty material solid)."},
